523
00:53:32,540 --> 00:53:33,246
Rym: Yeah, actually.

524
00:53:33,751 --> 00:53:38,398
Scott: As long as the other person can fight back and they're not, for example, tied up or something.

525
00:53:38,600 --> 00:53:43,640
Scott: In fact, to almost quote exactly, the number of people In which case it's not really a knife fight, it's more just of a knife torture or a knife assault.

526
00:53:43,640 --> 00:53:51,259
Rym: The number of people who will get cut badly in a knife fight is n+1 n being the number of knives involved in the fight.

527
00:53:53,220 --> 00:53:53,727
Scott: Well, it could be.

528
00:53:53,808 --> 00:53:59,730
Scott: I think it's just, you know, if there's one knife and like five people I could imagine all six people getting cut.

529
00:53:59,811 --> 00:54:08,260
Rym: I mean, basically if there's a knife in a room where violence is happening, I feel like a lot of people are going to get cut, regardless if the knife is even used in the fight.

530
00:54:09,280 --> 00:54:09,504
Scott: Right.

531
00:54:09,524 --> 00:54:18,540
Rym: Anyway, you know a movie where you see like an action hero holding a knife backwards, a lot of people like saw that in a movie once and think oh, that's a good way to cut your arm open.

532
00:54:18,580 --> 00:54:19,631
Rym: That's a good way to get cut.

533
00:54:20,096 --> 00:54:25,752
Rym: But you know you see like two people having a knife fight in a movie and the knives are hitting each other a bunch like it's a sword fight.

534
00:54:26,257 --> 00:54:35,993
Rym: The way knife fights that actually happen in the real world were described to me, and I got to see some footage of like security camera footage of knife fights that are involved in investigations.

535
00:54:36,478 --> 00:54:37,650
Rym: Imagine the opposite of that.

536
00:54:37,953 --> 00:54:39,793
Rym: Almost every time the knife moves, it cuts someone.

537
00:54:39,995 --> 00:54:41,550
Rym: It's not like you think in the movies.

538
00:54:41,611 --> 00:54:43,004
Rym: Knife fights are real bad.

539
00:54:43,025 --> 00:54:43,065
Rym: No.

540
00:54:43,874 --> 00:54:48,945
Scott: And you know, it's like Rym cut his finger a tiny bit in the kitchen.

541
00:54:49,006 --> 00:54:52,540
Rym: That was a traumatic emergency room stitches like big problem.

542
00:54:52,943 --> 00:54:53,146
Scott: Right.

543
00:54:53,207 --> 00:54:57,719
Scott: And in the knife fight you're going to, everyone will suffer several such cuts at minimum.

544
00:55:00,313 --> 00:55:01,085
Scott: One is bad enough.

545
00:55:01,186 --> 00:55:09,711
Scott: It's like imagine being there in the emergency room with like three or seven or and big or it's like no, don't don't mess it.

546
00:55:09,792 --> 00:55:10,338
Scott: Don't do it.

547
00:55:10,419 --> 00:55:10,863
Scott: Just run.

548
00:55:10,964 --> 00:55:12,197
Scott: If there's a knife fight, run.

549
00:55:12,217 --> 00:55:14,478
Scott: If you're far away from the knife, it can't cut you.

550
00:55:16,528 --> 00:55:18,159
